course: dictionary
lesson: 3809
title: Forerunners: the ones who came first
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: A forerunner is a person or thing that came before another and led the way for it. Look inside the word for clues: fore means before, and runner is the one that goes first. «The abacus was a forerunner of the calculator.» The abacus came first, and the calculator grew from it.
explain: Test your meaning by swapping it into the sentence. Try "The abacus was an early version of the calculator." It still makes sense, so your meaning is right. The words "a forerunner of" are the clue that one thing led to another.
explain: A forerunner can also be a sign that something is about to happen. Dark clouds can be a forerunner of a storm, because they warn you that rain and wind are coming soon.
fact: A forerunner is a person or thing that came before another and led the way for it.
fact: «The abacus was a forerunner of the calculator.»
fact: Babbage's engines were forerunners of computers, and the penny-farthing was a forerunner of the modern bicycle.
fact: Look for the phrases «a forerunner of» and «the forerunner to» to spot the link between two things.
fact: A forerunner can also be a sign that something is about to happen.
exercise: «The abacus was a forerunner of the calculator.» What is a forerunner? | *Something that came before and led the way for another | Something you forget very quickly | A kind of calculator used in shops | Something that comes after and is much newer
exercise: The penny-farthing was a forerunner of the modern bicycle. Which one came first? | The modern bicycle | *The penny-farthing | They were made on the same day | Neither one was ever made
exercise: Copy the word from «The abacus was a forerunner of the calculator» that names the older invention. | of | *abacus | forerunner | calculator
test: «Prince Dmytro built a fortress on the island, often seen as a forerunner of the Zaporizhian Sich.» What does forerunner suggest here? | A folk song about a prince | A fortress with no walls | *Something that came before and led to the Zaporizhian Sich | Something that was built after the Sich
test: Which phrase is a clue that you are reading about a forerunner? | once upon a time | *the forerunner to | at the end of the day | with a loud bang
exam: Dark clouds can be a forerunner of a storm. What does a forerunner tell you here? | That it is a sunny day | That the clouds are very old | *That a storm is about to happen | That the storm has already ended
